Artifact 2 — Codebook and Schema
Scale-Transition Annotation Graphs (STAG): Codebook and Machine-Readable Schema

This artifact is the operational instrument of the STAG framework. It is self-contained: it states the field list, the permitted value sets, the semantic validation rules, and the machine-readable schemas. The main paper (Artifact 1) refers to this artifact for field-by-field specifications and for the rule numbers used in the main text.

A.1 Node tuple
A node N is the tuple N = (S, M, G).

S, system scope: the scope-nesting position declared in the model reference.

M, model or formalism: the Hamiltonian, Lagrangian, or equivalent formal object under which the description is generated.

G, granularity: the annotation granularity declared before annotation begins.

Domain D is a partition-relative annotation attribute, not an identity component.

The domain fields are:

domain_id

partition_id

partition_version

Regime, purpose, validity regime, solution-method class, primary observable, and domains spanned are attributes.

A.2 Display labels
The seven display labels are:

STAG-Discovered, abbreviated STAG-DISC

STAG-Definitional, abbreviated STAG-DEF

STAG-None, abbreviated STAG-NONE

STAG-Intra, abbreviated STAG-INTRA

STAG-Intra-Definitional, abbreviated STAG-INTRA-DEF

STAG-Intra-Non_definitional, abbreviated STAG-INTRA-ND

STAG-Unclassified, abbreviated STAG-UNC

All seven are extension-tier and derived. evidential_anchoring accompanies every display label and takes the value not_applicable for non-STAG-Discovered labels.

